# Client-side routes, served the application shell so a deep link and a reload
# both reach the reader.
#
# Never replace these with `/* /index.html 200`. Cloudflare Pages applies a
# _redirects rule "regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming
# request", so a catch-all would answer /content/latest.json, every
# /content/editions/*.json, and every hashed asset with the HTML shell — the
# reader would then fail to parse its own edition as JSON. Add a line per route
# instead.
/edition /index.html 200
/edition/* /index.html 200
